# Implementation Plan - Scalable MySQL Auth with RBAC

Convert the current backend to use MySQL and implement a robust, scalable authentication/authorization system using JWT Refresh Tokens and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - We are switching from PostgreSQL to MySQL. Ensure you have a MySQL instance available.
> - The role system is designed to be granular (Roles + Permissions) to support future extensibility as requested.

## Proposed Changes

### Database & Prisma

#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///c:/mundrisoft/demo/fullstack/server/prisma/schema.prisma)
- Change datasource provider to `mysql`.
- **Proposed Scalable Schema**:
  ```prisma
  model User {
    id            String         @id @default(uuid())
    email         String         @unique
    password      String
    name          String?
    is_active     Boolean        @default(true)
    roles         UserRole[]
    refreshTokens RefreshToken[]
    resetTokens   PasswordResetToken[]
    created_at    DateTime       @default(now())
    updated_at    DateTime       @updatedAt
  }

  model Role {
    id          String           @id @default(uuid())
    name        String           @unique // SUPER_ADMIN, SUPPORT_ADMIN, WEBSITE_USER
    description String?
    permissions RolePermission[]
    users       UserRole[]
  }

  model Permission {
    id          String           @id @default(uuid())
    name        String           @unique // e.g., "manage_users", "view_admin_panel"
    description String?
    roles       RolePermission[]
  }

  model UserRole {
    user_id String
    role_id String
    user    User   @relation(fields: [user_id], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
    role    Role   @relation(fields: [role_id], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
    @@id([user_id, role_id])
  }

  model RolePermission {
    role_id       String
    permission_id String
    role          Role       @relation(fields: [role_id], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
    permission    Permission @relation(fields: [permission_id], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
    @@id([role_id, permission_id])
  }

  model RefreshToken {
    id         String   @id @default(uuid())
    token      String   @unique @db.VarChar(500)
    user_id    String
    user       User     @relation(fields: [user_id], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
    expires_at DateTime
    revoked_at DateTime?
    created_at DateTime @default(now())
  }

  model PasswordResetToken {
    id         String   @id @default(uuid())
    token      String   @unique
    user_id    String
    user       User     @relation(fields: [user_id], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
    expires_at DateTime
    created_at DateTime @default(now())
  }
  ```


### Authentication & Security

#### [NEW] Authentication Service
- **Signup**: User registration with default 'WEBSITE_USER' role.
- **Signin**: Issue Access Token (short-lived) and Refresh Token (long-lived, stored in DB).
- **Logout**: Revoke Refresh Token from DB.
- **Forgot/Reset Password**: Implement token-based password reset flow (using `PasswordResetToken` model).

#### [NEW] Security Middleware
- **JWT Verification**: Validate access tokens.
- **RBAC Middleware**: Check if user has required role/permission for specific routes.
- **Input Validation**: Use `zod` for all request payloads.
- **Rate Limiting**: Prevent brute force on auth endpoints.

